{"name":"Taffeta Tint","hex":"#f3e0eb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"taffeta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A crisp, smooth woven fabric made from silk or synthetic fibers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taffeta"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taffeta","blocks":[{"text":"Taffeta is a crisp, smooth, plain woven fabric made from silk, nylon, cuprammonium rayons, acetate, or polyester. The word came into Middle English via Old French and Old Italian, which borrowed the Persian word tāfta (تافته), which means \"silk\" or \"linen cloth\". As clothing, it is used in ball gowns, wedding dresses, and corsets, and in interior decoration, for curtains or wallcovering. It tends to yield a stiff cloth with a starched appearance that holds its shape better than many other fabrics and does not sag or drape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Woman%27s_Dress_LACMA_M.2007.211.35_%283_of_7%29.jpg/330px-Woman%27s_Dress_LACMA_M.2007.211.35_%283_of_7%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffeta"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg/500px-Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg/1280px-Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg/500px-Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink taffeta evening coat designed by Sybil Connolly","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg"}],"sounds":{"taffeta":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav.ogg"}],"tint":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tint.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikiped